    "body": "Triage, checked on `main` 8f30bee. This is two different asks, with very different costs.\n\n**1. A path that generated with warnings: mark the moves in the viewport.** Small, and the data is already there.\n- Every verify warning names its move: `Warning::Gouge { at }`, `ShankHit { at, part }`, `RapidInStock { at }`, `FixtureHit { at, .. }`, `Crossing { moves }`, `Envelope { at, .. }` (`crates/sim/src/verify/types.rs`). The list is cached with the path (`model::toolpath_of(..).warnings`).\n- Today the only surface is text. The op page folds the list into one line per kind (`operations::fold_warnings`: \"shank/holder at move 84 collides...\") and the browser row shows a count. The viewport draws the path in its normal feed, rapid and plunge colours, so the user has to count moves to find number 84.\n- A fix: paint the warned moves in the palette's gouge colour (`colorvision::Semantic::gouge`, already colour-vision aware), and make each folded warning line clickable to frame its first move. The program-level gouge already gets a located marker in the Deviate view (`shell.rs` reads `dev.max_gouge_at`), so there's a precedent.\n\n**2. A generation that was refused: show a path anyway.** Large, and a design call.\n- A refused `generate` returns `Err` and caches nothing: `OpStatus` is only `Never`, `Ok` or `Stale`. There's no partial path to draw, and generators stop at the first refusal.\n- Showing one would need a per-generator contract (return the path built so far plus the refusal), and a rule that such a path can never post. A cheaper middle ground is to draw the *place* a refusal names. Many already carry one, for example #260's \"two holes stand 15.15 mm apart on the row at Y=-55.50\".\n\nSuggest splitting: part 1 as its own issue a contributor can pick up, and part 2 as a research issue (which generators, what contract, how it stays unpostable).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
